version: v0.1.1
date-released: "2026-09-01"
keywords:
  - empirical legal studies
  - preventive law
  - legal drafting
  - corpus linguistics
  - statutory abrogation
  - Florida law
abstract: >-
  Empirical preventive law: measuring which drafting formulations draw
  litigation and which survive it, over a local corpus of 10.8M US judicial
  opinions joined to versioned state statutes. Classifiers are deterministic
  where possible and ship with measured precision and recall; every study
  reports its exclusion funnel with counts.

# GitHub reads this file to render a "Cite this repository" button, and Zenodo
# reads .zenodo.json at release time. Both must name the same ORCID, because the
# point of the identifier is that independent systems assert the same link
# rather than the author asserting it in one place.
#
# The CONCEPT doi is used here on purpose. 10.5281/zenodo.22247377 always resolves to the
# newest version; the version doi for this release is 10.5281/zenodo.22247378. Cite the
